Below is a simple example of an **interactive rotating card** using only HTML and CSS.  
When you hover over the card, it will rotate 180° around its Y‑axis (you can change the axis or angle if you wish).

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* Container that holds the front and back faces */
.card-wrapper {
    perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    margin: 50px auto;
}

/* The actual card element */
.card {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Enables 3D transforms on children */
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;/* Smooth animation */
}

/* Front face of the card */
.front,
.back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hides the reverse side when rotated */
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* Styling for the front face */
.front {
    background: #fff;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #333;
}

/* Styling for the back face */
.back {
    background: #f8f9fa;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* Initially hide behind the front */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: #555;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate the card */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front content -->
        <div class="front">
            <p>Front Side</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back content -->
        <div class="back">
            <p>Back Side</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a 3D perspective so the rotation looks realistic. |
| `.card` | Holds both faces and performs the rotation. |
| `.front`, `.back` | Each face of the card. `backface-visibility: hidden` ensures the hidden side isn’t visible during rotation. |
| `transform: rotateY(180deg)` | Rotates the back face to be initially hidden. |
| `.card:hover` | Triggers the rotation when the mouse hovers over the card. |

Feel free to replace the text inside `<p>` tags with images, icons, or any other content you like. You can also adjust the dimensions, colors, or rotation angle to fit your design.
